      Describes the types of trust boundaries implemented by Google Chrome and Firefox.
    </a:Description><a:Hidden>false</a:Hidden><a:Id>SE.TB.B.TMCore.NonIEB</a:Id><a:ImageLocation>Before label</a:ImageLocation><a:ImageSource>iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAABGdBTUEAALGPC/xhBQAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAABl0RVh0U29mdHdhcmUAQWRvYmUgSW1hZ2VSZWFkeXHJZTwAAABGSURBVDhPY/hPIWBQ9Ev6z2jqDccPnr0ESxArzoDMAeEDZy+DFRIrDjeAVDCcDIDyyQajgTioAhGEQekdHx+bGIUGeP8HAJ4fIfJijo6MAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC</a:ImageSource><a:ImageStream i:nil="true"/><a:Name>Other Browsers Boundaries</a:Name><a:ParentId>GE.TB.B</a:ParentId><a:Representation>BorderBoundary</a:Representation><a:Shape i:nil="true"/></a:ElementType></a:StandardElements><a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>S</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Spoofing</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>T</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Tampering</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>R</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Repudiation</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>I</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Information Disclosure</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>D</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Denial Of Service</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>E</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>A</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Abuse</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory></a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatMetaData><IsPriorityUsed>true</IsPriorityUsed><IsStatusUsed>true</IsStatusUsed><PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Title</Name><Label>Title</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ae1169ad-d70d-5c30-b1ff-e7f34ab676a5</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatCategory</Name><Label>Category</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id i:nil="true"/></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string><b:string>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>StateInformation</Name><Label>Justification</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>6c35d7f8-4667-5e8e-8819-d071a6418afa</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>InteractionString</Name><Label>Interaction</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id>1a1fad58-ca84-57e1-8358-0a7556d9121d</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string><b:string>Medium</b:string><b:string>Low</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string><b:string>FR6 Timely response to events</b:string><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string><b:string>SL 2</b:string><b:string>SL 3</b:string><b:string>SL 4</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ExistingControls</Name><Label>Existing Countermeasures</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ExistingControls</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ScenarioRef</Name><Label>HAZOP or Cyber HAZOP Reference</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ScenarioRef</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ConsequenceCategory</Name><Label>Consequence Category</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>Health and safety</b:string><b:string>Environment</b:string><b:string>Production loss</b:string><b:string>Equipment damage</b:string><b:string>Product quality</b:string><b:string>Regulatory or reputation</b:string><b:string>Financial</b:string></Values><Id>ConsequenceCategory</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Severity</Name><Label>Consequence Severity (1-5)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>1 - Negligible</b:string><b:string>2 - Minor</b:string><b:string>3 - Moderate</b:string><b:string>4 - Major</b:string><b:string>5 - Catastrophic</b:string></Values><Id>Severity</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Likelihood</Name><Label>Likelihood (1-5)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>1 - Rare</b:string><b:string>2 - Unlikely</b:string><b:string>3 - Possible</b:string><b:string>4 - Likely</b:string><b:string>5 - Almost certain</b:string></Values><Id>Likelihood</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>RiskRating</Name><Label>Current Risk</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>Critical 20-25</b:string><b:string>High 12-19</b:string><b:string>Medium 6-11</b:string><b:string>Low 1-5</b:string></Values><Id>RiskRating</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Tolerable</Name><Label>Within Tolerable Risk</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>Yes</b:string><b:string>No</b:string></Values><Id>Tolerable</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Treatment</Name><Label>Risk Treatment</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not decided</b:string><b:string>Mitigate</b:string><b:string>Accept</b:string><b:string>Transfer</b:string><b:string>Avoid</b:string></Values><Id>Treatment</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PlannedActions</Name><Label>Planned Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>PlannedActions</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ResidualRisk</Name><Label>Residual Risk</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>Critical 20-25</b:string><b:string>High 12-19</b:string><b:string>Medium 6-11</b:string><b:string>Low 1-5</b:string></Values><Id>ResidualRisk</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Ownership</Name><Label>Action Owner</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>Ownership</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>DueDate</Name><Label>Due Date</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>DueDate</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Validation</Name><Label>Verification Evidence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>Validation</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></PropertiesMetaData></a:ThreatMetaData><a:ThreatTypes><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>The flow from {source.Name} to {target.Name} crosses a zone boundary but is not filtered by a firewall or conduit device, so the zones are not really separated and an attacker in one zone can reach the other freely.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(((source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.PhysicalProcess') or (flow.Medium is 'Removable media or file transfer')) or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (flow.ThroughConduitDevice is 'Unknown' or flow.ThroughConduitDevice is 'No')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The flow from {source.Name} to {target.Name} crosses a zone boundary but is not filtered by a firewall or conduit device, so the zones are not really separated and an attacker in one zone can reach the other freely.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Route every inter-zone flow through a conduit device (firewall, data diode, DPI gateway) with deny-by-default rules that allow only this documented flow. Record the conduit in the zone and conduit drawing.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0886 Remote Services; T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; 3-3 SR 5.2; 3-2 ZCR 3; 2-1 NET 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of segmentation; Attack spread</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{source.Name} to {target.Name} crosses a zone boundary without a conduit device</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Commands or setpoints sent to {target.Name} use a protocol without authentication across a zone boundary. Anyone who gets a foothold on the path or in the source zone can send valid-looking commands.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(((source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.PhysicalProcess') or (flow.Medium is 'Removable media or file transfer')) or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Unknown' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'None') and (flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Commands or setpoints sent to {target.Name} use a protocol without authentication across a zone boundary. Anyone who gets a foothold on the path or in the source zone can send valid-looking commands.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Allow only the specific function codes or services needed at the conduit (protocol-aware firewall). Restrict which hosts may send writes. Use secure protocol variants where the installed equipment supports them. Monitor for writes from unexpected hosts.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1692.001 Unauthorized Message: Command Message; T0831 Manipulation of Control</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 3.1; 3-3 SR 5.2; 2-1 NET 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control; Safety; Production loss</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unauthenticated control traffic from {source.Name} to {target.Name} crosses zones</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} is not encrypted where it leaves the zone. Process data, tag names or credentials can be captured and used to plan an attack.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes' or (source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.PhysicalProcess') or (flow.Medium is 'Removable media or file transfer')) or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Unknown' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'None' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Integrity only')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-I01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} is not encrypted where it leaves the zone. Process data, tag names or credentials can be captured and used to plan an attack.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Encrypt flows leaving the zone where confidentiality matters (TLS, IPsec tunnel between sites). Never send passwords in cleartext. Classify plant data to decide where encryption is needed.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0842 Network Sniffing; T0882 Theft of Operational Information</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 4.1; 2-1 DATA 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Plant data between {source.Name} and {target.Name} readable in transit</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} is on the business network, which is far more exposed to phishing and ransomware. This flow is a path from a compromised office PC or server into the plant.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.EnterpriseIT') and (flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{source.Name} is on the business network, which is far more exposed to phishing and ransomware. This flow is a path from a compromised office PC or server into the plant.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Terminate business-to-plant flows in the industrial DMZ. Do not allow business hosts to connect to Level 1 and 2 directly. Use separate accounts and domains for IT and OT. Review this flow in the conduit rule set.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0886 Remote Services; T0884 Connection Proxy; T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; 3-3 SR 5.2; 2-1 NET 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Production loss; Ransomware spread</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Attack path from the business network via {source.Name} to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} receives traffic directly from the business network, a cloud service or an untrusted network, bypassing the supervisory and DMZ layers.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.EnterpriseIT' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Cloud') or (flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.OT.Internet' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.OT.Cloud' or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN'))) and (target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} receives traffic directly from the business network, a cloud service or an untrusted network, bypassing the supervisory and DMZ layers.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Broker the connection through the DMZ or a remote access gateway. Make any access from higher levels read-only. Re-check the zone model and the SL-T for this zone.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0883 Internet Accessible Device; T0886 Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; 3-3 SR 5.2; 3-2 ZCR 3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Controller {target.Name} reachable from outside the plant</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} is reached over the Internet or a cellular or WAN carrier network. Exposed industrial services are routinely found by Internet-wide scanning and attacked within days.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.OT.Internet' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.OT.Cloud' or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN')) and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-I02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} is reached over the Internet or a cellular or WAN carrier network. Exposed industrial services are routinely found by Internet-wide scanning and attacked within days.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use a private APN or VPN for cellular links. Block inbound connections from the Internet. Check your public address ranges regularly for exposed OT services.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0883 Internet Accessible Device; T0846 Remote System Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 3-3 SR 1.13; 2-1 NET 3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} discoverable from the Internet or a carrier network</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>The link between {source.Name} and {target.Name} depends on an external carrier or WAN. An outage, a jamming attack or an attack on the provider stops remote control and monitoring.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The link between {source.Name} and {target.Name} depends on an external carrier or WAN. An outage, a jamming attack or an attack on the provider stops remote control and monitoring.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Define how the remote site behaves on loss of communication (local autonomous control, safe state). Provide a backup path for essential sites. Include the carrier in incident and continuity plans.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1695.002 Block Communications: Ethernet; T0827 Loss of Control</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.1; 2-1 AVAIL 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of view; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Carrier or WAN outage cuts {source.Name} from {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Cellular routers and WAN links are often installed by vendors or contractors and not managed by the site. They can bypass the firewall and give a direct way into the zone.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.Router') or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Cellular routers and WAN links are often installed by vendors or contractors and not managed by the site. They can bypass the firewall and give a direct way into the zone.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Keep an inventory of all external connections (CM 1). Manage routers centrally: change default passwords, disable unused services, restrict management access. Search regularly for unauthorised modems and routers.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0883 Internet Accessible Device</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 2-1 CM 1; 2-1 NET 3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of segmentation</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unmanaged or undocumented WAN or cellular connection at {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Plant wireless networks can be reached from outside the fence. A rogue access point or a device with a stolen key can join the network used by {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((flow.Medium is 'Wireless') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WirelessIF is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-S01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Plant wireless networks can be reached from outside the fence. A rogue access point or a device with a stolen key can join the network used by {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use strong wireless authentication and manage join keys. Separate wireless into its own zone behind a firewall. Monitor for rogue access points (NET 2).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0860 Wireless Compromise; T0887 Wireless Sniffing</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.6; 2-1 NET 2; 2-4 SP.04</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Rogue device on the wireless network used by {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Remote access accounts are a favourite target. Phished, reused or leaked credentials let an attacker log in as {source.Name} from anywhere.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess') or (flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.OT.Internet' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.OT.Cloud' or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN')) and (source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-S02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Remote access accounts are a favourite target. Phished, reused or leaked credentials let an attacker log in as {source.Name} from anywhere.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require multi-factor authentication for all remote access. Use individual named accounts, never shared vendor accounts. Restrict access by source address and time window. Review remote access logs.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.13; 2-1 NET 3; 2-4 SP.07</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Stolen or reused credentials used for remote access by {source.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} can connect whenever it wants, without approval or supervision. A compromise of the vendor or integrator becomes a compromise of the plant.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') and ((source is 'GE.EI' and (source.AccessManagement is 'Unknown' or source.AccessManagement is 'Always on or unsupervised')) or (flow.PermanentConnection is 'Unknown' or flow.PermanentConnection is 'Yes'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{source.Name} can connect whenever it wants, without approval or supervision. A compromise of the vendor or integrator becomes a compromise of the plant.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Enable third-party access only on request, approved by operations and time-limited. Record or supervise sessions. Limit each third party to the assets it supports. Include security requirements in service contracts (2-4).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0886 Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.6; 2-1 NET 3; 2-4 SP.07</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Always-on or unsupervised access by {source.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker with remote desktop or remote access to {target.Name} can operate the process exactly as an operator or engineer would, for example changing chemical dosing setpoints.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool')) and ((source is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') or flow is 'SE.DF.OT.RemoteDesktop' or (flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.OT.Internet' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.OT.Cloud' or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker with remote desktop or remote access to {target.Name} can operate the process exactly as an operator or engineer would, for example changing chemical dosing setpoints.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Do not allow remote control of operator stations without on-site approval. Prefer view-only remote access. Alarm on remote sessions. Keep engineering limits and interlocks in the controller, not only in the HMI.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0823 Graphical User Interface; T0831 Manipulation of Control</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.1; 3-3 SR 1.13; 2-1 NET 3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Environmental; Manipulation of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Remote takeover of the operator or engineering session on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Work done by {source.Name} (new equipment, upgrades, maintenance) may reintroduce default passwords, open ports or unpatched software if security requirements are not part of the contract and acceptance tests.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Work done by {source.Name} (new equipment, upgrades, maintenance) may reintroduce default passwords, open ports or unpatched software if security requirements are not part of the contract and acceptance tests.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Specify IEC 62443-2-4 capabilities in contracts. Check security settings at factory and site acceptance tests. Require hand-over documentation of accounts, ports and software versions.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0862 Supply Chain Compromise; T1694.001 Insecure Credentials: Default Credentials</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>2-4 SP.02; 2-4 SP.03; 2-1 ORG 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Changes by {source.Name} to {target.Name} not covered by security requirements</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Security patches for {target.Name} are not installed or their status is unknown, so publicly known vulnerabilities can be exploited.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.PatchStatus is 'Unknown' or target.PatchStatus is 'Patches pending')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Security patches for {target.Name} are not installed or their status is unknown, so publicly known vulnerabilities can be exploited.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Keep a patch status register for every asset (COMP 3). Qualify and install vendor-approved patches in planned outages. Where patching must wait, document compensating controls such as stricter filtering at the conduit.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T0890 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 3.2; 2-1 COMP 3; 2-4 SP.11</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Known vulnerabilities on {target.Name} not patched</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} runs software or firmware that the vendor no longer supports. Vulnerabilities will stay open for the rest of its life in the plant.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and ((target is 'GE.P' and (target.PatchStatus is 'End of life or unpatchable')) or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.LegacyOS is 'Yes'))) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} runs software or firmware that the vendor no longer supports. Vulnerabilities will stay open for the rest of its life in the plant.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Isolate the asset in its own zone with strict conduit rules. Disable unused services. Add monitoring. Plan replacement in the asset lifecycle budget and record the accepted risk.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T0890 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>2-1 COMP 3; 3-2 ZCR 5; 2-1 CM 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} is end of life and cannot be secured by patching</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} has no malware protection or application allow-listing, so malware arriving by network, USB or a vendor laptop runs unchecked.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.MalwareProtection is 'Unknown' or target.MalwareProtection is 'No')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} has no malware protection or application allow-listing, so malware arriving by network, USB or a vendor laptop runs unchecked.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use application allow-listing or vendor-qualified anti-malware (COMP 2). Keep signatures updated through an OT update server. Block execution from removable media.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0863 User Execution; T0847 Replication Through Removable Media; T1701 Command and Scripting Interpreter</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 3.2; 2-1 COMP 2; 2-4 SP.10</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise; Production loss</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Malware can run on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} was installed with vendor defaults: unused services and ports open, default settings and no security baseline applied.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.Hardening is 'Unknown' or target.Hardening is 'No')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} was installed with vendor defaults: unused services and ports open, default settings and no security baseline applied.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Apply the site hardening baseline (vendor security guide, CIS-type benchmark). Disable unused ports, services and accounts. Check configuration against the baseline after every change (CM 1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T1694.001 Insecure Credentials: Default Credentials</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.7; 3-3 SR 7.6; 2-1 COMP 1; 2-4 SP.03</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} runs with default or unhardened configuration</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Logins on {target.Name} use default, shared or generic accounts. Passwords are widely known, rarely changed and cannot be tied to a person.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.UserAccounts is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SharedAccounts is 'Unknown' or target.SharedAccounts is 'Yes')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-S03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Logins on {target.Name} use default, shared or generic accounts. Passwords are widely known, rarely changed and cannot be tied to a person.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Change all default passwords at commissioning. Use individual accounts where the system supports them. Where shared accounts cannot be avoided, control the password in a vault and log who checked it out.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1694.001 Insecure Credentials: Default Credentials; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.1; 2-1 USER 1; 2-4 SP.09</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Default, shared or generic accounts in use on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Accounts of staff who left, former contractors or commissioning engineers often stay active on {target.Name} for years and can be misused.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.UserAccounts is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-S04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Accounts of staff who left, former contractors or commissioning engineers often stay active on {target.Name} for years and can be misused.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Run a joiner-mover-leaver process that covers OT systems. Review OT accounts at least yearly. Set expiry dates on contractor accounts. Remove commissioning accounts at hand-over.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.3; 2-1 USER 1; 2-4 SP.09</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Leavers' and contractors' accounts still active on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Security events from {target.Name} are not collected or reviewed, and its network traffic is not monitored. An intrusion could continue for months before anyone notices.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SecurityMonitoring is 'Unknown' or target.SecurityMonitoring is 'No')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-R01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Security events from {target.Name} are not collected or reviewed, and its network traffic is not monitored. An intrusion could continue for months before anyone notices.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Forward security events to a central log server or SIEM. Deploy passive OT network monitoring on the zone. Define who reviews alerts and how fast (EVENT 1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0872 Indicator Removal on Host; T0846 Remote System Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 6.2; 2-1 EVENT 1; 2-4 SP.08</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR6 Timely response to events</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Detection; Recovery time</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Attacks on {target.Name} would not be detected</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>No tested backup exists for {target.Name}, or the restore has never been tried. After ransomware, a wiper or a hardware failure the plant may run without it for days or weeks.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.BackupTested is 'Unknown' or target.BackupTested is 'No')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>No tested backup exists for {target.Name}, or the restore has never been tried. After ransomware, a wiper or a hardware failure the plant may run without it for days or weeks.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Back up programs, configurations and system images (AVAIL 2). Keep an offline copy. Test restores on a schedule and record the restore time. Store installation media and licences.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0809 Data Destruction; T0828 Loss of Productivity and Revenue</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.3; 2-1 AVAIL 2; 2-4 SP.12</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Production loss; Recovery time</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} cannot be restored quickly after ransomware or failure</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>The capability security level (SL-C) of {target.Name} is lower than the target security level (SL-T) of its zone, or has not been checked. The zone cannot reach its target without extra measures.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.MeetsZoneSLT is 'Unknown' or target.MeetsZoneSLT is 'No')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The capability security level (SL-C) of {target.Name} is lower than the target security level (SL-T) of its zone, or has not been checked. The zone cannot reach its target without extra measures.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Compare SL-C with SL-T for every asset (3-2 ZCR 5). Where SL-C is lower, add compensating countermeasures (filtering, monitoring, physical protection) and document them, or replace the asset.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 3-2 ZCR 5; 3-2 ZCR 6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Residual risk above tolerable</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Security capability of {target.Name} is below the zone target</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Ransomware entering the plant can spread across Windows hosts through shared accounts, file shares and remote services, encrypting {target.Name} and forcing a shutdown.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Ransomware entering the plant can spread across Windows hosts through shared accounts, file shares and remote services, encrypting {target.Name} and forcing a shutdown.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Limit lateral movement: host firewalls, no shared admin accounts, separate OT domain. Keep offline backups. Prepare and exercise a plan to run the process without the affected hosts.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0809 Data Destruction; T0828 Loss of Productivity and Revenue; T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; 2-1 AVAIL 2; 2-1 EVENT 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Production loss; Financial</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Ransomware spreads to {target.Name} and stops operations</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>If {target.Name} is manipulated, the process could exceed safe limits (overdosing, overpressure, overflow). The question is whether non-programmable safeguards still prevent the hazard.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') and (flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.AssetConsequence is 'Not assessed' or target.AssetConsequence is 'Major' or target.AssetConsequence is 'Catastrophic'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>If {target.Name} is manipulated, the process could exceed safe limits (overdosing, overpressure, overflow). The question is whether non-programmable safeguards still prevent the hazard.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Run a cyber-HAZOP or consequence analysis for this controller. Confirm that the worst cases are covered by safeguards an attacker cannot change remotely (mechanical relief, hard-wired trips, independent SIS). Record the scenario reference.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0831 Manipulation of Control; T0836 Modify Parameter; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 3.6; 3-2 ZCR 5; IEC 61511-1 8.2.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Environmental; Equipment damage</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Cyber attack on {target.Name} could drive the process to a hazardous state</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Changes to logic, setpoints or configuration of {target.Name} are not controlled by management of change. A malicious or careless change would not be noticed until the process misbehaves.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') and (flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Changes to logic, setpoints or configuration of {target.Name} are not controlled by management of change. A malicious or careless change would not be noticed until the process misbehaves.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Apply management of change to OT changes. Compare running logic with the approved version regularly. Use controller key switches or write-protection. Keep a change log with who, what and why (CM 1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0889 Modify Program; T0843 Program Download; T0836 Modify Parameter</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.1; 2-1 CM 1; 2-4 SP.06</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Product quality</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unauthorised or unmanaged change to logic or configuration of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>A cyber attack on the safety system {target.Name} could disable trips or change trip points, so a hazardous event is no longer prevented (TRITON).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SafetyRelated is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>A cyber attack on the safety system {target.Name} could disable trips or change trip points, so a hazardous event is no longer prevented (TRITON).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Carry out the SIS security risk assessment required by IEC 61511-1 8.2.4. Keep the SIS in its own zone. Use the key switch in Run, and control bypasses and maintenance overrides with procedures and alarms.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0880 Loss of Safety; T0837 Loss of Protection; T0889 Modify Program</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>IEC 61511-1 8.2.4; 2-4 SP.05; 3-3 SR 5.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Environmental</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Safety function {target.Name} disabled or altered by a cyber attack</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} accepts traffic from outside the safety zone. A compromise of the control system could reach the safety function, so the two layers are no longer independent.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.PhysicalProcess') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SafetyRelated is 'Yes'))) and (flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} accepts traffic from outside the safety zone. A compromise of the control system could reach the safety function, so the two layers are no longer independent.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Separate the SIS in its own zone with a dedicated conduit. Allow read-only traffic from the BPCS where possible. Keep the SIS engineering station inside the safety zone and disconnected when not in use.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0880 Loss of Safety; T0886 Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; IEC 61511-1 8.2.4; 2-4 SP.05</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Safety system {target.Name} reachable from the control zone</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>If {target.Name} is lost to an attack or failure, operators may not be able to run or safely shut down the process if no manual operating procedures exist or they are not practised.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA') and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>If {target.Name} is lost to an attack or failure, operators may not be able to run or safely shut down the process if no manual operating procedures exist or they are not practised.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Write and exercise procedures for running or shutting down the process without the control system. Provide local panels or hard-wired indications for critical values. Include the scenario in incident response exercises.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0829 Loss of View; T0815 Denial of View; T0827 Loss of Control</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.1; 2-1 AVAIL 1; 2-1 EVENT 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of view; Safety; Production loss</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Loss of view or control on {target.Name} without a manual fallback</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker who suppresses or floods alarms on {target.Name} can hide an attack or an abnormal process condition from operators.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA') and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker who suppresses or floods alarms on {target.Name} can hide an attack or an abnormal process condition from operators.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Control alarm configuration and shelving through management of change. Monitor alarm settings for changes. Make critical alarms independent of the SCADA system where the consequence is high.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0878 Alarm Suppression; T0838 Modify Alarm Settings</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.1; 2-1 CM 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Alarms on {target.Name} suppressed or not acted on</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may be a single point of failure. An attack, a misconfiguration or a failed update could cut communication for a whole zone.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} may be a single point of failure. An attack, a misconfiguration or a failed update could cut communication for a whole zone.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Provide redundancy for network devices that carry essential traffic. Back up device configurations. Test changes before applying them and keep spare units.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service; T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.1; 2-1 AVAIL 1; 2-1 AVAIL 2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of view; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Failure of {target.Name} cuts essential communication</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Firewall rules on {target.Name} tend to grow over time: any-any rules, temporary vendor rules that stay, unused rules. Each one weakens the zone separation.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Firewall rules on {target.Name} tend to grow over time: any-any rules, temporary vendor rules that stay, unused rules. Each one weakens the zone separation.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Review conduit rules at least yearly and after projects. Require a documented reason and owner for every rule. Remove temporary rules on an expiry date. Alert on rule changes.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0884 Connection Proxy; T0885 Commonly Used Port</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 2-1 NET 1; 2-4 SP.03</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of segmentation</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Conduit rules on {target.Name} too permissive or not reviewed</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Vulnerability scans or discovery tools run from {source.Name} can crash or slow fragile controllers like {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.EnterpriseIT' or source is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or source is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Vulnerability scans or discovery tools run from {source.Name} can crash or slow fragile controllers like {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Exclude Level 0 to 2 devices from IT scanning. Use passive asset discovery in OT. Test any active query in a lab first and run it only in agreed windows.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.1; 2-1 ORG 2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of availability; Production loss</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>IT security scanning from {source.Name} disrupts {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>USB drives, contractor laptops and other transient devices connected to {target.Name} are a common way malware reaches air-gapped or isolated plant networks (Stuxnet).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.RemovableMedia') or (flow.Medium is 'Removable media or file transfer'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>USB drives, contractor laptops and other transient devices connected to {target.Name} are a common way malware reaches air-gapped or isolated plant networks (Stuxnet).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Control portable media and transient devices (COMP 1): scan at a kiosk before use, use company-owned media only, block unknown USB devices, and keep a register of transient devices and their owners.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0847 Replication Through Removable Media; T0864 Transient Cyber Asset</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.3; 2-1 COMP 1; 2-4 SP.10</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Malware brought to {target.Name} on USB media or a visiting laptop</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} may not recognise phishing, social engineering or pretext phone calls. A single successful lure can give an attacker valid access to {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') and (source is 'GE.EI' and (source.SecurityTraining is 'Unknown' or source.SecurityTraining is 'No'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-S05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{source.Name} may not recognise phishing, social engineering or pretext phone calls. A single successful lure can give an attacker valid access to {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Give OT-specific security awareness training to operators, engineers and contractors (ORG 1). Teach staff to verify unexpected remote support requests. Report suspicious events without blame.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0865 Spearphishing Attachment; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>2-1 ORG 1; 2-4 SP.01</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{source.Name} tricked into giving access to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>A disgruntled, coerced or careless {source.Name} could misuse legitimate privileges on {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E12</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>A disgruntled, coerced or careless {source.Name} could misuse legitimate privileges on {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Grant least privilege by role (USER 2). Require approval and a second person for critical changes. Review privileged actions. Include OT roles in background checks and leaver processes.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.1; 2-1 USER 2; 2-1 ORG 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Insider misuse of privileges by {source.Name} on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Because {target.Name} uses shared accounts, it is not possible to tell which person made a change or issued a command.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SharedAccounts is 'Unknown' or target.SharedAccounts is 'Yes'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-R02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Because {target.Name} uses shared accounts, it is not possible to tell which person made a change or issued a command.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use individual accounts, or log who used a shared account and when. Keep an operator action journal and retain logs long enough for investigations.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts; T0872 Indicator Removal on Host</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.8; 3-3 SR 1.1; 2-1 USER 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Forensics; Compliance</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Actions by {source.Name} on {target.Name} cannot be traced to a person</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Engineering projects, network drawings, backups and process history on {target.Name} tell an attacker how the plant works and where it is weak.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.ProjectFiles' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.Backup' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.HistorianDB')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-I03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Engineering projects, network drawings, backups and process history on {target.Name} tell an attacker how the plant works and where it is weak.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Classify plant documentation and restrict access (DATA 1). Encrypt backups and laptops. Control what is replicated to the business network and to vendors.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0882 Theft of Operational Information; T0811 Data from Information Repositories</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 4.1; 2-1 DATA 1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Plant drawings, programs or process history stolen from {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>If {target.Name} is reachable from the same network and accounts as the systems it protects, ransomware will encrypt or delete the backups too.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.DS' and target.OfflineCopy is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.DS.OT.Backup' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-D07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>If {target.Name} is reachable from the same network and accounts as the systems it protects, ransomware will encrypt or delete the backups too.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Keep at least one offline or immutable copy. Use separate credentials for the backup system. Test restores from the offline copy.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0809 Data Destruction</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 7.3; 2-1 AVAIL 2; 2-4 SP.12</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Recovery time; Production loss</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Backups in {target.Name} encrypted or deleted together with the plant systems</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Events reach {target.Name} but nobody is responsible for reviewing them, or there is no plan for what to do when an OT alert fires.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-R03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Events reach {target.Name} but nobody is responsible for reviewing them, or there is no plan for what to do when an OT alert fires.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Assign alert review to a named team with response times. Write an OT incident response plan with operations, safety and the vendors. Exercise it at least yearly (EVENT 1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0872 Indicator Removal on Host</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 6.1; 2-1 EVENT 1; 2-4 SP.08</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR6 Timely response to events</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Detection; Recovery time</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Security alerts from {source.Name} not reviewed or acted on</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Someone with physical access to {target.Name} (remote station, field cabinet, open plant area) can connect a laptop, insert media, reset the device or tamper with wiring.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.PhysicalProcess' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.FieldDevice3P') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.PhysicallyExposed is 'Unknown' or target.PhysicallyExposed is 'Yes')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-T10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Someone with physical access to {target.Name} (remote station, field cabinet, open plant area) can connect a laptop, insert media, reset the device or tamper with wiring.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Lock cabinets and buildings, use door and cabinet intrusion alarms, and monitor remote sites (ORG 3). Disable unused ports. Alarm on device restarts and link changes.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0864 Transient Cyber Asset; T0816 Device Restart/Shutdown</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 2.3; 2-1 ORG 3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Equipment damage</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Physical access to {target.Name} at an unattended or open location</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>The plant depends on {source.Name}. If that service is compromised, it may push commands or configuration into the plant or leak plant data.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Cloud')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>PL-E13</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The plant depends on {source.Name}. If that service is compromised, it may push commands or configuration into the plant or leak plant data.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Recommended Countermeasure(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Keep cloud connections outbound-only and read-only where possible. Require local approval for any write from the cloud. Include the provider in supplier risk assessment and contracts.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0862 Supply Chain Compromise; T1692.001 Unauthorized Message: Command Message</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 and IEC 61511 Reference(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 2-1 ORG 1; 2-4 SP.02</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Compromise of cloud or vendor service {source.Name} affects {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType></a:ThreatTypes></KnowledgeBase><Profile><PromptedKb xmlns=""/></Profile></ThreatModel>